# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment state (production.md P-16)
#
# Everything an application writes at runtime lives inside its own folder and is
# never committed: the environment files hold secrets, the data directories hold
# user content, and the certificate store must be root-only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
compose.override.yaml
# ...except Zulip's, which carries the derived-image build and is part of the
# deployment: `include` loads it explicitly from compose.yaml.
!Zulip/compose.override.yaml
*.local.yaml
# Secrets are ignored by file, not by directory: excluding the directory makes a
# per-file negation impossible, and the *.example placeholders must be committed
# (they are the deployment's template for each secret).
**/secrets/*
!**/secrets/*.example
**/data/
**/logs/
acme.json
# Mailcow's own checkout, once its tooling has cloned it into Mailcow/. The tree
# is upstream's, not this project's, so the clone is ignored whole rather than
# file by file — a list of names has to be maintained against every upstream
# release, and the one thing it must never do is let the clone's contents be
# committed as though Workcenter had written them. Its nested .git would
# additionally make this repository treat Mailcow/ as an embedded repository.
#
# `/*` and not `/`: Mailcow/ itself has to stay traversable, because a negation
# can only re-include a path whose parent directories are not themselves excluded.
/Mailcow/*
# The three files Workcenter authors for the deployment, and the only ones that
# belong in this repository. `sogo-custom/` is Workcenter's own directory — the
# clone does not carry it — so the directory is re-included along with the file,
# since re-including the file alone is not enough to reach it.
!/Mailcow/docker-compose.override.yml
!/Mailcow/mailcow.conf.example
!/Mailcow/sogo-custom/
!/Mailcow/sogo-custom/workcenter-theme.js
# Application runtime state that the deployment folders bind-mount.
OnlyOffice/lib/
OnlyOffice/db/
Filebrowser/office-cache/
# The local certificate and any internal CA: private keys, never committed.
Traefik/certs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Workcenter
# Never commit generated artefacts, secrets or runtime data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules
/dist
/coverage

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and generated configuration
# Every application folder keeps its own .env and secrets; none are tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example
# Secrets are ignored by file, not by directory: excluding the directory itself
# makes a per-file negation impossible, and the *.example placeholders must be
# committed — they are the deployment template for each secret.
**/secrets/*
!**/secrets/*.example
**/*.local.yaml
**/*.local.yml
acme.json
**/acme.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime data owned by integrated applications
# Volumes are bind-mounted inside each application's folder.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/data/
**/logs/
**/office-cache/
**/database/
**/rabbitmq/
**/redis/
**/postgres/
**/media/
**/templates/

# Broker token store
user-data/broker/
user-data/config-backups/
# Runtime files of the manual verification harness (scripts/e2e.sh)
user-data/e2e/
# The shell configuration the harness generates for a run, mounted over
# user-data/conf.yml and Traefik/dynamic/middlewares.yml by compose.test.yaml.
# The tracked files are the operator's.
user-data/conf.test.yml
Traefik/dynamic/middlewares.test.yml
# The identity configuration the harness generates for a run, mounted over
# Filebrowser/config.yaml and Traefik/dynamic/dashboard.yml. These carry the
# run's OIDC client secret in plain text, so ignoring them is not tidiness: an
# untracked-looking `config.test.yaml` in a commit would publish a credential
# that Authentik still honours (P-16, O-13.1).
Filebrowser/config.test.yaml
Traefik/dynamic/dashboard.test.yml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test and tooling artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/test-results
/playwright-report
/e2e/test-results
/e2e/playwright-report
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Generated per run by scripts/e2e.sh: the local test CA mounted into Mailcow's
# php-fpm, which is where the OIDC exchange happens. Never committed.
Mailcow/docker-compose.test.yml

# The developer's pull-request guidance and PR exclusion files which are ignored
# as a directory. The directory is deliberately used to exclude all contents from
# a PR. Within the gitignore folder is the PR-guide.md, which names the repository,
# the base branch and authentication, and contains everything needed to push to
# this project. Nothing inside gitignore-PR belongs in history or online repository.
gitignore-PR/
